Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: retain EC100 gadget workarounds

Keep the existing EC100 DWC2 changes together as downstream workarounds.
This combines the previous reset and bulk OUT patches without changing
kernel behavior; it does not establish a shared root cause.

Reconnect with no session-valid signal:

On EC100's debug/download connector, PHY BVALID and DWC2 BSESVLD remain
low even during working gadget traffic. Unplug suspends the controller
without reporting a session disconnect. The reset on reconnect then
disconnects the old gadget session, putting it in L3, but skips core
reinitialization because BSESVLD is low. EP0 setup requests subsequently
fail with -EAGAIN.

For a fixed peripheral, accept the received USB reset as sufficient to
reinitialize a previously connected gadget. Retain the connected guard
and the existing session-valid requirement for OTG operation. This does
not fake VBUS status, change host mode, or treat suspend as disconnect.
Reconnect tests passed with this workaround, but its suitability as a
generic DWC2 fix remains unresolved. The upstream RFC was closed.

Bulk OUT receive guard (experimental):

Boot-connected Ethernet can stop receiving when the host sends bulk OUT
traffic before the gadget netdevice opens. Delaying host traffic until
the netdevice is ready avoids the observed failure. The precise
controller failure is still unconfirmed.

Explicitly set NAK when configuring a bulk OUT endpoint, so making the
endpoint active does not rely on its previous NAK state while there is no
receive request. dwc2_hsotg_start_req() already clears NAK after
programming the receive buffer and transfer size. Leave EP0, IN and
periodic endpoints unchanged.

Retain this guard as part of the working local stack, not as a proven fix.
The successful guarded test received bulk traffic late and did not
exercise the failing early-traffic sequence; an unguarded late-traffic
test also passed. The experimental upstream PR was closed. Missing
session-valid signaling does not establish that this guard is necessary.

Link: https://github.com/armbian/linux-rockchip/pull/579
Link: https://github.com/armbian/linux-rockchip/pull/580

---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -3792,7 +3792,13 @@
 		/* Reset device address to zero */
 		dwc2_clear_bit(hsotg, DCFG, DCFG_DEVADDR_MASK);
 
-		if (usb_status & GOTGCTL_BSESVLD && connected)
+		/*
+		 * Fixed peripherals may lack usable VBUS sensing. A bus reset
+		 * still requires reinitialization after disconnecting the old
+		 * session, otherwise EP0 remains inactive in L3.
+		 */
+		if (connected && ((usb_status & GOTGCTL_BSESVLD) ||
+				  hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL))
 			dwc2_hsotg_core_init_disconnected(hsotg, true);
 	}
 
@@ -4171,6 +4177,9 @@
 
 	case USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_BULK:
 		epctrl |= DXEPCTL_EPTYPE_BULK;
+		/* Keep OUT NAKed until start_req() installs a receive buffer. */
+		if (!dir_in)
+			epctrl |= DXEPCTL_SNAK;
 		break;
 
 	case USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_INT:
